  "question": {
    "text": "<p>The figure shows two solid discs with radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi></math>&nbsp;respectively. If mass per unit area is the same for both, what is the ratio of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>I</mi></math> of bigger disc around axis <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi></math> (Which is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8869;</mo></math> to the plane of the disc and passing through its centre) of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>I</mi></math> of smaller disc around one of its diameters lying on its plane? Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi></math> is the mass of the larger disc.</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mi>I</mi></math> stands for a moment of inertia)</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/abcc741d-63a6-4ca9-bfa9-496b647386c5-image.png\" style=\"width: 224px; height: 212px;\" /></p>",
    "image": null
